check::lock_state_screen

  × the lock's `state wide` cannot start from `screen`
   ╭─[lock_state_screen.strand:7:16]
 6 │   open: <-> locked
 7 │   state wide = screen.width
   ·                ──────┬─────
   ·                      ╰── read once for every monitor
 8 │   text "locked"
   ╰────
  help: a lock's `state` is one for the lock on every monitor (so a password typed on one is typed
        on all): start it from a value, and read `screen` in props or a `let` instead
